Hypothesis: The method reports BAD_IMPLEMENTED_TYPE ('can only implement interfaces') by iterating functionType.getImplementedInterfaces() without guarding against cyclic/self-referential inheritance. For recursive cases, getImplementedInterfaces() recursively concatenates super constructor interfaces and can both surface non-interface constructors in loops and trigger infinite recursion/stack overflow during subtype/property checks.

